<title>GERMANY: German glass maker suspected in wage fraud probe.</title>
<headline>German glass maker suspected in wage fraud probe.</headline>
<dateline>DORTMUND, Germany 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German glass maker Flachglas AG is being investigated for fraud and tax evasion in connection with extra wages paid to employees who were later laid off, the state prosecutor's office said on Friday.</p>
<p>One employee was held for questioning after police searched company offices in Gelsenkirchen and Witten on Wednesday, officials said.</p>
<p>Flachglas is suspected of raising wages to enable workers slated for layoffs to qualify for higher unemployment benefits.</p>
<p>The scheme allegedly cost the Federal Labour Office several hundred thousand marks in lost revenues.</p>
<p>Flachglas eliminated more the 500 jobs in the last 12 months, helping lift profits even though sales have stagnated at around 1.5 million marks ($976,000).</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150 ($ = 1.535 German Marks)</p>
